<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113710" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χείρ-ωμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is subdued, a conquest,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δούλης θανούσης, εὐμαροῦς χειρώματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1326
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>deed of violence,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφαντος ἔρρει θανασίμῳ χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					560
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a work wrought by the hand,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυμβοχόα χ.,</span> of earth thrown up (v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυμβοχόος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1027
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
